   "daf": "20b",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "וְהֵם אוֹמְרִים הוֹצִיאוּהָ וְכוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא — דְּדִילְמָא מֵתָה. לְמֵימְרָא דְּמֵת אָסוּר בְּמַחֲנֵה לְוִיָּה?",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: «And» the people standing in the Temple «say: Remove her,» so that she does not render the Temple courtyard impure. The Gemara explains: «What is the reason» for this? It is «lest she die» there immediately and render the women’s courtyard, where she drinks the water, impure. The Gemara asks: «Is this to say that a corpse is prohibited» from being «in» the women’s courtyard, which has the same status as the «Levite camp» in the desert?"
  }
